          "distinct": false,
          "id": "7d2e4463839871b58f4f33eadc154ab655628ff7",
          "message": "feat(ci): M4 feature-OFF perf-neutrality CI proof gate (sq-pntvh.8) [OPUS-4.8] (#1386)\n\n* feat(ci): M4 feature-OFF perf-neutrality CI proof gate (sq-pntvh.8) [OPUS-4.8]\n\nThree-leg gate proving the `vectorized` feature-OFF build is compile-time absent\nand artifact-deterministic:\n- Leg 1 (feature-resolution guard): cargo metadata check that `vectorized` is absent\n  from the resolved default workspace feature set and the wasm profile — catches the\n  feature-unification trap before any build.\n- Leg 2 (artifact exact-equality): wasm bundle built feature-OFF, size asserted == the\n  pinned bench/perf-baseline.json floor (zero delta, stricter than the 2% ratchet in\n  bench.yml). Any accidental vectorized code would change the bundle size.\n- Leg 3 (cfg-audit): script asserting every `vectorized` module registration and\n  evaluator call site in lib.rs / exec.rs is under `#[cfg(feature = \"vectorized\")]`.\n- Tripwires: leg-1 guard rejects a synthetic metadata fixture with vectorized enabled;\n  leg-2 comparator rejects a perturbed baseline byte.\n\nHonest scope: proves compile-time absence + artifact byte-determinism; does NOT assert\nruntime perf neutrality (EC2-gated). Gate feeds the ci-summary aggregator (no change to\nthe required `gate` check or to ci-summary.yml). Land first (before sq-pntvh.5/4/y5ew5)\nto guard the rest of the M4 epic while seams are wired.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(ci): leg 2 exact-equality uses feature_off_exact pin, not ratchet floor (sq-pntvh.8) [OPUS-4.8]\n\nRoot cause: check-vectorized-feature-off.py --leg2 compared the CI-built wasm size\nagainst wasm_bundle_bytes.floor (1399703), which is the 2%-band ratchet lower bound\nused by bench.yml — NOT the exact current size. Main drifted +127 bytes within-band\n(floor 1399703 -> actual 1399830) after the floor was committed, so the exact-equality\ncheck against the floor failed on every CI run.\n\nFix: add a dedicated `feature_off_exact` field to bench/perf-baseline.json (1399830,\nmeasured on this branch: cargo build --profile release-wasm -p sparq-wasm\n--target wasm32-unknown-unknown with no --features vectorized, aarch64 work box).\ncheck_leg2() now compares against feature_off_exact, not floor. A missing\nfeature_off_exact is a hard error, so the field cannot silently drift.\n\nThe ratchet floor (1399703) is UNCHANGED — it still gates bench.yml at ±2%.\n\nLocal verification:\n- leg 2 PASSES: measured 1399830 == feature_off_exact 1399830\n- tripwire (1399831) still FAILS: delta=+1 byte caught\n- All 5 unit tests in scripts/tests/test_vectorized_feature_off.py PASS\n- YAML valid; actionlint clean; gate aggregator untouched; SHA-pins intact\n- Legs 1 and 3 unaffected\n\nA legitimate wasm change must update BOTH floor AND feature_off_exact in the same PR\ndiff; the script's error message now explicitly instructs this.\n\n🤖 SPARQ agent — CI/infra fix for PR #1386\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(ci): re-pin feature_off_exact to CI x86_64 value 1399110 (sq-pntvh.8) [OPUS-4.8]\n\nThe previous fix pinned feature_off_exact=1399830 from an aarch64 work-box\nbuild. CI x86_64 (ubuntu-latest) measures 1399110, so the exact-equality\ncheck still fails with delta=-720. This commit corrects the pin to the CI\nx86_64 measurement.\n\nChanges:\n- bench/perf-baseline.json: feature_off_exact 1399830 -> 1399110; comment\n  updated to state this is the CI x86_64 value and MUST be re-pinned from\n  a CI run (never a local aarch64 measurement)\n- scripts/check-vectorized-feature-off.py: self-test tripwire updated to\n  use 1399110 (the live value leg 2 will compare against)\n- scripts/tests/test_vectorized_feature_off.py: both leg-2 tests updated\n  to pinned_exact=1399110; tripwire (1399111) correctly rejects; all 5\n  tests pass locally\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(ci): fail-closed leg2 on missing wasm pin + gate test-file path (sq-pntvh.8) [OPUS-4.8]\n\nAddress Copilot review on the vectorized-feature-OFF gate:\n\n- check_leg2: fail-closed when bench/perf-baseline.json omits the\n  wasm_bundle_bytes metric. The comparison loop only iterates keys\n  present in the floor, so an edited/corrupted baseline that dropped\n  the pin would yield zero violations and silently PASS, disabling the\n  exact-equality gate. Now a missing pin is a hard failure. Adds a\n  regression tripwire (test_leg2_rejects_missing_pin).\n- paths-filter: add scripts/tests/test_vectorized_feature_off.py so a\n  PR editing only the gate's test suite triggers the legs (previously\n  rust_changed=false -> all three legs skipped, updated test logic\n  unexercised).\n- wording: \"pinned floor\" -> \"feature_off_exact\" in the Leg 2 step\n  name, the job-2 header comment, and the CLI --leg2 help, so a failure\n  in CI is not misread as a floor/ratchet issue (the gate deliberately\n  compares against feature_off_exact, not the floor).\n\nLegs 1/3 and the CI x86_64 feature_off_exact pin (1399110) unchanged.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Jesse Wright <jmwright.045@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
