          "distinct": false,
          "id": "2e201417b7733db50e4c1dc3b478b98e63d8f5df",
          "message": "docs(research): CI structural speedup design — engine decomposition, feature-matrix pyramid, profiles, cache topology, heavy-lane placement (sq-6vshe) [FABLE-5] (#1396)\n\nDesign record for the STRUCTURAL CI wins beyond the in-flight tactical\nfixes (sq-fmx4u selection, per-job caching, sq-piapk coverage shard):\npositions on the sparq-engine split (measure-first, decision rule),\na 3-tier feature-matrix pyramid replacing ~50 per-feature legs, the\nCI build-profile trio, prime-on-main cache topology with poisoning\ndiscipline, and heavy-lane per-PR/nightly placement. Prioritized\ndisjoint child beads sq-6vshe.1-.7. No implementation.\n\nCo-authored-by: Jesse Wright <jmwright.045@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-03T02:42:33Z",
